id: pm-rust-yz76
title: Absorb pm 2026.8.7 codec and workspace contracts
description: "Re-prove the Rust-native read and create slice against the newly published pm CLI and SDK 2026.8.7, including the @toon-format/toon 4.1.1 codec change, and update every pinned compatibility gate without introducing a runtime bridge."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: compatibility,interop,rust,sdk,toon
created_at: "2026-08-07T12:13:40.150Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T12:22:54.029Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T12:22:53.657Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T12:22:53.657Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: An exact fixture generated by the official @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 proves canonical TOON item and create-history bytes for ambiguous scalar and tag values; Read list get and create acceptance run against a fresh 2026.8.7 tracker and the mature companion tracker without copying private data; COMPATIBLE_PM_VERSION documentation and CI health/merge-driver pins identify 2026.8.7 while pm-changelog stays on its independently latest published version; The implementation remains entirely Rust at runtime and all cross-platform tests doc coverage audit PM health and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage gates pass
definition_of_ready: pm-rust-5tey is merged; pm 2026.8.7 is published on npm and GitHub; its release notes and packaged SDK contracts are available read-only
value: Prevents agents from writing a stale or subtly incompatible workspace format immediately after a canonical codec release
impact: Keeps the independent implementation honest and exposes any codec or envelope drift before broader mutation work
outcome: The supported native slice is demonstrably interoperable with the current published pm CLI and SDK
why_now: pm 2026.8.7 changed the canonical JavaScript TOON codec and became the current public contract today
parent: pm-rust-u4al
reviewer: maintainer
risk: high
confidence: medium
sprint: 2026-08-compatibility
release: 0.1.0-alpha.3
resolution: "Updated the declared compatibility baseline and CI pins, installed the 2026.8.7 merge fence, and locked exact official SDK TOON and history bytes into the Rust acceptance suite."
expected_result: "The native Rust read and create slice exactly matches published pm 2026.8.7 contracts while retaining complete test, branch, and doc coverage."
actual_result: "Official SDK fixture matched exact TOON, history, and hash; 36 tests and exact 897/897 line, 111/111 function, 1320/1320 region, and 134/134 branch coverage passed; fresh-tracker acceptance plus a 614-item aggregate-only companion differential passed; cargo audit, strict rustdoc, pm validate, and pm health passed."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T12:13:50.391Z",codex,"Published baseline verified on 2026-08-07: npm @unbrained/pm-cli latest is 2026.8.7 and GitHub release v2026.8.7 was published at 10:47:23Z. The release upgrades @toon-format/toon to 4.1.1 and adds caller-carried output sessions plus normalized row contracts; only behavior intersecting the currently supported read/create slice belongs in this tranche."
  "2026-08-07T12:19:44.735Z",codex,"Official SDK fixture generation used @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 with PM_WORKSPACE_RECIPE_SCHEMA, a fixed 2026-08-07T10:06:30.183Z clock, explicit ID and author, extensions disabled, and ambiguous scalar/tag values. The Rust create path matched the resulting TOON bytes, JSONL patch order, and 6eb97257 after-hash exactly on its first characterization run. Fresh 2026.8.7 tracker acceptance then read the Rust-created item and history and passed validate plus read-only health. Mature private-tracker differential comparison matched all 614 items on id/status/type/title/priority/parent; only aggregate counts are recorded here."
  "2026-08-07T12:20:24.434Z",codex,"The first pm 2026.8.7 validation run found tracked merge-fence drift: extensions/** must be excluded from item merging while .managed-extensions.json uses pm-json. Applied the canonical pm merge install output rather than hand-authoring patterns. This is a data-safety compatibility fix; clone-local drivers were already healthy."
  "2026-08-07T12:21:26.310Z",codex,"The first aggregate pm test run passed Rust tests, coverage, and rustdoc, then correctly refused the health link because its default schema sandbox contained zero items while the source tracker contained five. Replaced that link with explicit tracker context; this is linked-test configuration, not a pm-rust or pm-cli defect."
files[4]{path,scope,note}:
  .gitattributes,project,pm 2026.8.7 extension-asset merge fence
  .github/workflows/ci.yml,project,Exact published pm CLI health and merge-driver pins
  src/lib.rs,project,Published compatibility version constant
  tests/create_contract.rs,project,Official SDK byte-for-byte create fixture
tests[4]:
  - command: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --all-targets --all-features
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 300
  - command: cargo +nightly-2026-08-06 llvm-cov --locked --branch --all-targets --all-features --json --output-path coverage-branch.json
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 300
  - command: npm exec --yes --package=@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.7 -- pm health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 300
    pm_context_mode: tracker
  - command: "RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"--document-private-items -D missing-docs\" cargo +1.90.0 doc --locked --all-features --no-deps"
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 300
